{
  "_comment": [
    "Who may be named as the medical reviewer of a blog post, and on what.",
    "",
    "This file exists to make one specific mistake impossible: putting a",
    "clinician's name and credential on content outside their licensed scope of",
    "practice. A byline that says 'Medically reviewed by Dr. X, D.C.' attaches",
    "that person's licence to the claims in the post. If the post is about",
    "testosterone dosing and the reviewer is a chiropractor, that is a",
    "scope-of-practice problem for them and a substantiation problem for us.",
    "",
    "Two rules, both enforced by scripts/blog/editorial_guard.py, which fails",
    "the daily-publish build rather than warning:",
    "  1. A reviewer may only be named on categories in their 'scopes' list.",
    "  2. A category marked requiresPrescriber accepts only a reviewer whose",
    "     'prescribes' is true.",
    "",
    "A post with no reviewer renders NO reviewer byline. That is the correct",
    "behaviour and the default. Never add an entry to 'reviews' for a review",
    "that did not actually happen — the byline is a factual claim about a named",
    "person on a specific date.",
    "",
    "2026-09-13 policy change (DaChé, COO): the clinical reviewer need not be the prescriber. Dr. Tim Pepin, D.C. reviews all categories; bylines say 'Clinically reviewed by', never 'Medically reviewed'. Reviews below were recorded on his confirmation that he has reviewed all posts; date = posting date.",
    "2026-09-14 date correction: 95 entries carried the POST'S publish date, the earliest 2026-01-05 — months before this registry existed and before any review was recorded. Per the note above, what actually happened is that Dr. Pepin confirmed on 2026-09-13 that he had reviewed the existing content, so those entries now read 2026-09-13. The policy is unchanged; only dates that asserted a review on a day it did not happen were corrected. Posts published from 2026-09-13 onward are reviewed the day they publish, so posting date and review date genuinely coincide and are left as they are."
  ],
